Option 1: Terminal (Quickest)
Open two terminal tabs in Rider and run these:

Start the Server first:
powershell
$env:DOTNET_ROOT = "$HOME\.dotnet"; & "$HOME\.dotnet\dotnet.exe" run --project Teledon.Server\Teledon.Server.csproj
Start the Client:
powershell
$env:DOTNET_ROOT = "$HOME\.dotnet"; & "$HOME\.dotnet\dotnet.exe" run --project Teledon.Client\Teledon.Client.csproj
Option 2: Rider Run Configurations
To run directly via the Run button in Rider:

Configure .NET CLI:
Go to File | Settings | Build, Execution, Deployment | Toolset and Build.
Ensure the .NET CLI executable path is set to: C:\Users\Caius\.dotnet\dotnet.exe.
Server Configuration:
Right-click Teledon.Server project -> Edit Configurations.
Ensure Teledon.Server is selected as the startup project.
Client Configuration:
Right-click Teledon.Client project -> Edit Configurations.
Ensure Teledon.Client is selected.
Compound Launch (Optional):
Go to Run | Edit Configurations.
Click + -> Compound.
Add both Teledon.Server and Teledon.Client. This allows you to start both with one click!
IMPORTANT

Always ensure the Server is fully started ("Server started. Waiting for clients...") before launching the Client.